## Spec wording — explicit "Coordination is out of scope"

Silence is not achievable: removing the existing "Cross-worktree
coordination" section without a replacement leaves a hole that invites
reinvention. Replace it with this paragraph:

> ## Coordination is out of scope
>
> %erg v1 describes what a ticket is, not how concurrent agents or
> worktrees share access to one. There is no claim file, no lock, no
> doing-but-mine state. If two agents need to avoid stepping on each
> other, they observe out-of-band signals — typically a git branch
> whose name contains the ticket ID — and coordinate there. Such
> conventions are workflow choices, not properties of this format.

## Migration

1. **In-flight `.wip` files.** None in this clone (`/home/user/git-erg/.git/`
   has no `ticket-wip/`). Other clones may have them; they become
   harmless orphans inside `.git/` (never committed). The ticket's
   "delete if exists" step is *advisory* — it cannot reach other
   developers' machines.
2. **`erg ready --json` contract break.** The `wip` field disappears.
   Known consumer: IDH skills (per 0006 §D and 0008). Atomic switch is
   acceptable because the field was always optional and never carried
   semantic guarantees. Document in release notes; downstream readers
   should already tolerate a missing key.
3. **`erg graph` annotation change.** `, claimed` suffix disappears.
   Plaintext output only — no JSON contract.
4. **Skill removal.** `/ticket-claim` and `/ticket-release` slash
   commands disappear. Anyone with muscle memory will get a "command
   not found"; release note is enough.
5. **Atomic vs. window.** Atomic. `.wip` was never a hard lock so there
   is no consistency to preserve. One PR removes all sites; the next
   `erg validate` run confirms.
6. **Cross-worktree visibility shift.** Today, `erg ready` on machine A
   won't show a ticket claimed on machine B's worktree. After 0013,
   `erg ready` may show the same ticket on both machines — nothing in
   the binary checks `git branch --all`. This is an explicit decision,
   not an oversight: deconfliction returns to the agents/humans, by
   design.
7. **Verification.**
   - `grep -rni 'ticket-wip\|\.wip\b\|claim\|release' rules/ docs/ claude/ bin/ tickets/tools/go/` returns zero hits.
   - `erg ready --json | jq '.[] | keys'` shows no `wip` key.
   - `go test ./tickets/tools/go/...` and `make test` green.
   - `erg validate tickets/` green.

## Companion changes (separate tickets/PRs)

- **Close 0006, file modularization ticket.** 0006 bundled
  claim+release+close+modularize+godoc. `close` shipped in PR #7;
  claim/release vanish here. The remaining work (Go modularization +
  godoc) has nothing structurally in common with the original — file
  it as a fresh ticket and close 0006 with reason
  `"superseded — close shipped in #7; claim/release dropped per 0013;
  modularization+godoc moved to 0014"`. This matches the
  close-and-fork pattern from PR #9 (closing 0009/0011 as
  work-already-shipped).
- **0007 ("install erg on PATH")** has no real dependency on 0006 —
  only narrative motivation. Drop its `Blocked-by: 0006` outright when
  this lands.
- **0008 ("erg pick command")** depends on the modularization, not
  claim/release. Re-point its `Blocked-by:` at the new modularization
  ticket.

## Sequencing with 0012

Land **0013 first**. It is mechanical and decisively scoped; 0012 still
has open design questions (path-vs-header, fate of `pending`). 0012's
rationale §5 explicitly cites `.git/ticket-wip/` as the reason `doing`
can be dropped — 0013 invalidates that argument either way, so 0012's
body needs amendment regardless. Landing 0013 first lets 0012 reference
"no Status enum, no WIP — the only state machine left is closed/not-closed"
as a clean simplification.

## Out of scope

- Any branch-naming convention or "WIP detector" command. Stale-branch
  hygiene and remote-branch handling are user concerns, not the spec's.
- Status enum changes (covered by 0012).
- Modularization of `tickets/tools/go/main.go` (covered by the new
  companion ticket).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] All 12 changesites listed in §Scope updated; no remaining hits in
      `grep -rni 'ticket-wip\|\.wip\b\|claim\|release' rules/ docs/ claude/ bin/ tickets/tools/go/`
- [ ] `rules/tickets.md` carries the new "Coordination is out of scope"
      paragraph in place of the deleted section
- [ ] `erg ready --json` no longer emits a `wip` field
- [ ] `erg graph` no longer emits `, claimed`
- [ ] Validator passes on all tickets
- [ ] 0006 closed and modularization ticket filed (companion PR)
- [ ] 0007 unblocked; 0008 re-pointed at the modularization ticket
